1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,675
Mobile Gaming: The Largest Gaming Platform.

2
00:00:03,625 --> 00:00:16,237
Mobile gaming continues to dominate the global games industry in 2026, generating over $110 billion in annual revenue and reaching more than 3.5 billion players worldwide.

3
00:00:16,237 --> 00:00:25,125
Tencent's Honor of Kings remains the highest-grossing game on the planet, with its battle arena gameplay sustaining a massive paying audience across Asia.

4
00:00:25,125 --> 00:00:36,125
HoYoverse's Genshin Impact and its successor Zenless Zone Zero continue to perform strongly, each regularly appearing in the top-grossing charts across both iOS and Android stores.

5
00:00:36,125 --> 00:00:49,925
Smartphone hardware improvements have narrowed the visual gap between mobile and console games, with titles like Call of Duty Mobile and the newly released Resident Evil 9 Mobile Edition demonstrating console-quality graphics on modern devices.

6
00:00:49,925 --> 00:00:55,212
The rise of cloud gaming streaming onto phones has further blurred platform boundaries.

7
00:00:55,212 --> 00:01:06,137
Emerging markets in Southeast Asia, Latin America, and Africa account for the largest share of new mobile players, driving growth as smartphone penetration increases globally.

